@startuml Give file access flow
title Give file access flow

actor "Owner User" as Owner
participant "Owner Mobile App" as OwnerApp
participant "API Gateway" as Gateway
participant "Auth Service" as Auth
participant "Permission Service" as Permission
database "Permission DB" as PermissionDB
queue "Event Bus / Kafka" as Kafka
participant "Sync Service" as Sync
database "Sync DB" as SyncDB
participant "Target User App" as TargetApp

Owner -> OwnerApp : Add read/edit access\nfor target user

OwnerApp -> Gateway : POST /files/{file_id}/permissions\nuser_id, permission
Gateway -> Auth : Validate token
Auth --> Gateway : owner_user_id

Gateway -> Permission : Grant access\nowner_user_id, target_user_id,\nfile_id, permission

Permission -> Permission : Check that owner_user_id can give access
Permission -> PermissionDB : Create permission record\nfile_id, target_user_id, permission
PermissionDB --> Permission : OK

Permission -> Kafka : FileShared event\nfile_id, owner_user_id,\ntarget_user_id, permission

Permission --> Gateway : access granted
Gateway --> OwnerApp : success
OwnerApp --> Owner : Access granted


Kafka ->> Sync : FileShared event
Sync -> SyncDB : Update that target user\nhas access for a new file
SyncDB --> Sync : OK

alt Target app is online
    Sync -> TargetApp : WebSocket notification\nnew shared file available
    note right of Sync
        Device Synchronization Flow
    end note
else Target app is offline
    note right of Sync
    Target user will receive this change
    when they open the app
    end note
end


@enduml